BT /F1 9 Tf 45 755 Td 11 TL (- GET /events/stats returns grouped severity and status counts.) Tj T* (- GET /metrics returns Prometheus exposition data.) Tj T* () Tj T* (EVENT-PROCESSOR) Tj T* (- GET /health and GET /metrics provide probe and monitoring surfaces.) Tj T* () Tj T* (DASHBOARD) Tj T* (- GET /health returns service health.) Tj T* (- GET / renders severity cards and recent processed events.) Tj T* () Tj T* (5. PROCESSING RULES) Tj T* (- security_alert events with critical or high severity generate notification messages.) Tj T* (- performance_metric events with cpu_percent above 90 receive alert=High CPU Usage.) Tj T* (- application_log messages containing ERROR or Exception receive needs_attention=true.) Tj T* (- Successful queue messages are acknowledged. Processing failures are now negatively) Tj T* (acknowledged and requeued, preventing silent loss.) Tj T* () Tj T* (6. PERSISTENCE AND DATA MODEL) Tj T* (The database initialization Job creates events and processed_events tables. events stores) Tj T* (critical/high events accepted synchronously by the ingestor. processed_events stores the) Tj T* (processor output used by the query API and dashboard. JSONB metadata preserves the full) Tj T* (event payload and derived fields. Timestamp and severity/status indexes support the primary) Tj T* (access patterns.) Tj T* () Tj T* (7. KUBERNETES DEPLOYMENT) Tj T* (The manifests define the event-monitoring namespace, Deployments for application workers,) Tj T* (StatefulSets for PostgreSQL/RabbitMQ/Redis, Services for internal discovery and selected) Tj T* (NodePort access, ConfigMaps, Secrets, probes, resource requests/limits, Ingress, and a) Tj T* (database initialization Job. The setup flow builds and pushes images, updates image registry) Tj T* (references, applies the namespace and workloads, waits for readiness, and supports port-) Tj T* (forwarding for local access.) Tj T* () Tj T* (kubectl get pods -n event-monitoring kubectl port-forward -n event-monitoring svc/event-) Tj T* (ingestor-service 8081:80 bash scripts/test-events.sh kubectl port-forward -n event-) Tj T* (monitoring svc/dashboard-service 8080:80) Tj T* () Tj T* (8. TERRAFORM AWS PRODUCTION DIRECTION) Tj T* (The Terraform area models a production-oriented AWS path with VPC, EKS, RDS PostgreSQL, and) Tj T* (Redis modules. This is distinct from the local Kubernetes manifests: the manifests run the) Tj T* (playground stack, while Terraform provisions cloud infrastructure intended to host or) Tj T* (support a production deployment. Review variables, credentials, state management,) Tj T* (networking, and secret handling before applying to an AWS account.) Tj T* () Tj T* (9. CI/CD AND OBSERVABILITY) Tj T* (The Jenkins pipeline builds service images, pushes them to a registry, deploys Kubernetes) Tj T* (resources, and includes operational stages for verification and rollback. Prometheus) Tj T* (configuration scrapes application metrics, while Grafana dashboard JSON provides) Tj T* (visualization. Metric families include events_received_total, events_processed_total, and) Tj T* (notifications_sent_total.) Tj T* () Tj T* (10. SECURITY AND RELIABILITY NOTES) Tj T* (- Default credentials exist in application fallbacks and development manifests; production) Tj T* ET
endstream
endobj
